      "side": 0,
      "message": "A new libavif fuzz test happened to run into the same crash, and I found the answer to James\u0027s question.\n\nThe `is_gradient_caching_for_hog_enabled(ppi-\u003ecpi)` function takes the current frame\u0027s frame type into account. Note the `frame_is_intra_only(\u0026cpi-\u003ecommon)` call:\n\n```\nstatic inline bool is_gradient_caching_for_hog_enabled(\n    const AV1_COMP *const cpi) {\n  const SPEED_FEATURES *const sf \u003d \u0026cpi-\u003esf;\n  return frame_is_intra_only(\u0026cpi-\u003ecommon) \u0026\u0026 !sf-\u003ert_sf.use_nonrd_pick_mode \u0026\u0026\n         (sf-\u003epart_sf.partition_search_type \u003d\u003d SEARCH_PARTITION) \u0026\u0026\n         (sf-\u003eintra_sf.intra_pruning_with_hog ||\n          sf-\u003eintra_sf.chroma_intra_pruning_with_hog);\n}\n```\n\nThis is fine when we decide whether we need to allocate the `td-\u003epixel_gradient_info` array for the current frame, which is the case in the `allocate_gradient_info_for_hog()` function because `allocate_gradient_info_for_hog()` is called before encoding every frame.\n\nHowever, this is problematic in the `av1_init_tile_thread_data()` function, because it is not called before only when the number of worker threads change (increase?).  So if we happen to call `av1_init_tile_thread_data()` when the current frame is an `INTER_FRAME`, then `is_gradient_caching_for_hog_enabled()` will return false so we won\u0027t allocate the `td-\u003epixel_gradient_info` array. Then we will dereference a null pointer when we encode a `KEY_FRAME`.\n\nGiven this understanding, we can check a condition that doesn\u0027t consider the current frame\u0027s frame type here, i.e., something like this:\n\n```\nstatic inline bool is_gradient_caching_for_hog_enabled_for_tile_thread_data(\n    const AV1_COMP *const cpi) {\n  const SPEED_FEATURES *const sf \u003d \u0026cpi-\u003esf;\n  return !sf-\u003ert_sf.use_nonrd_pick_mode \u0026\u0026\n         (sf-\u003epart_sf.partition_search_type \u003d\u003d SEARCH_PARTITION) \u0026\u0026\n         (sf-\u003eintra_sf.intra_pruning_with_hog ||\n          sf-\u003eintra_sf.chroma_intra_pruning_with_hog);\n}\n```",
